1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and it
flies all the way there,

3
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:29,360
to Kashiwa from gym class,
who was goofing around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for
staying just as full of energy.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,140
Where's the good energy?

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
Wherever I go, winning is the only way.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare: the unchanging townscape

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,900
is gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already gone down.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,940
Yakitori, hobari

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,820
Even just looking at it...

13
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat

14
00:00:57,460 --> 00:00:59,480
from the sosuitoro

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,720
taishakute

16
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:04,060
The sunset falls.

17
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:07,980
Tomorrow too

18
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,060
Why does it have to end?

19
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:11,460
Katsushika, Shibamata

20
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,660
Even happiness is lost

21
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:14,640
I realized

22
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm a fool

23
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,680
Yeah!

24
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:27,220
What's that, Ryo-chan?

25
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:32,500
It's an udon bowl:
instant udon noodles on top of rice.

26
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,660
Udon bowl?

27
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,920
That's not very balanced
nutritionally, is it?

28
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:38,780
But it's cheap, so that's good, right?

29
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:43,240
Do you think I do this because I like it?

30
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,420
Maybe it's the horse?

31
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:55,780
What?!

32
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,220
Ugh, come on!

33
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,220
Honest Ryo-san.

34
00:02:03,611 --> 00:02:10,700
I was an idiot for
following the old man's tip.

35
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,620
Ryo-chan!

36
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:16,360
Ryo-san! You idiot!

37
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,020
What did you do this time, Ryo-chan?

38
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:23,680
Come on, spit it out! Confess quietly!
What on earth did you do?!

39
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:26,940
Please calm down, Chief!

40
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:29,700
Be honest, what did you do?

41
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:32,740
Even if you say that, I have no idea...

42
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:37,820
There's no way the Police Commissioner
would summon you by name for nothing!

43
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,740
The Police Commissioner?

44
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:42,900
W-Police Commissioner?

45
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,200
Just hearing the name makes me tremble.

46
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,620
What did you do, Ryo-chan?

47
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,700
Did you remember?

48
00:02:55,700 --> 00:03:00,060
Could it be that they found out I drew the
commissioner's caricature on the patrol car?

49
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:01,920
What exactly did I do?

50
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,800
No, no, or maybe it's that one...

51
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,880
No, it might be that one.

52
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:08,220
Have I really done that many things?

53
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,820
What do I do? My heart's pounding.

54
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:13,920
Nothing to do with the sensō-ji, right?

55
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:14,820
But...

56
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:17,340
Anyway, come with me.

57
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:20,500
I'll take you with me and commit seppuku!

58
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,400
No, no, no!

59
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:23,760
I don't want to commit seppuku!

60
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:35,440
Commissioner, it's Ohara.

61
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:37,260
I've brought Ryotsu.

62
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,700
Come in.

63
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,040
Y-yes.

64
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:43,920
Excuse us.

65
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,440
We are truly, deeply sorry for this.

66
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:54,980
It is entirely my fault
for my lack of supervision.

67
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:57,220
Please, I beg you, forgive us.

68
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:59,700
Please, I beg you, forgive him.

69
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:01,700
Please, I beg you.

70
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:03,960
Lift your head, Ohara.

71
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,660
Actually, Ohara-kun,

72
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:11,520
today the Commissioner came in person
to commend Patrol Sergeant Ryotsu.

73
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:14,420
The Commissioner himself came all this way.

74
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:19,265
Hahaha, let me explain.
Patrol Sergeant Ryotsu,

75
00:04:19,315 --> 00:04:24,740
you helped an elderly man who fell off his bicycle the other day,
didn't you?

76
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:26,540
An elderly man?

77
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,720
Right.

78
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,820
Rya! Hey-chi!

79
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,060
Well then.

80
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,240
I've gone and done it again.

81
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,440
Help me, help me!

82
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,040
Who's laughing?

83
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,500
Are you all right, old man?

84
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:13,180
Ugh, I hit my hip.

85
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:17,700
I can't get up. Hang in there.

86
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:19,620
Here you go.

87
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:25,660
That's it, that's good, right?

88
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:32,540
Hey.

89
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:36,080
Hey, helping people up is part
of a police officer's job too.

90
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,800
Where's your home? I'll take you there.

91
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:42,420
It's that way.

92
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:45,940
Alright then.

93
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:54,140
I've got some business around here,
or rather over toward the Edogawa side.

94
00:05:55,660 --> 00:06:02,640
I'm on my way back, so, well, it's kind
of the same as your situation, I suppose.

95
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:05,700
I'm more of a freelance type of police officer,
you see.

96
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:21,180
Thanks, I'm sorry, you really saved me. Gramps,
you're getting old, so don't push yourself too hard.

97
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,940
Hahaha.

98
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:26,800
By the way, may I ask your name?

99
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,860
It's not worth mentioning,

100
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:30,440
but it's Kankichi Ryotsu.

101
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:31,540
See ya.

102
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:37,540
That elderly man was

103
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:39,500
one of the country's leading tycoons,

104
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:41,520
a super-rich man.

105
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:43,020
W-wealthy?

106
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:46,780
He was just a shabby old geezer.

107
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:48,500
The tycoon

108
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:53,060
dresses like that when he makes
surprise visits to his own company.

109
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:56,440
So that people don't judge others by appearance alone,
you see.

110
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:57,460
I see.

111
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:02,860
The tycoon was deeply moved by Ryotsu's performance,
you know.

112
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:06,100
In order to produce more
police officers like you,

113
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:11,340
he said he'd sponsor a
police recruitment commercial.

114
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:18,020
So, on the tycoon's recommendation,
you're going to appear in that commercial.

115
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:19,560
Me, Ryotsu? Really?

116
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,300
That's right.

117
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:23,900
So that you can set an
example for all police officers.

118
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,580
Do your best, all right?

119
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:28,280
Understood.

120
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:32,740
If that's the case, I'll take
responsibility and make sure he does it.

121
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,980
Speaking of rich people,

122
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:39,680
he's the one who built the Shōjiki
Group from nothing in his own lifetime.

123
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:42,360
Does he also have ties
with the Nagakawa Konzern?

124
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:43,660
Of course.

125
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,580
He should also know my daddy.

126
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:52,540
Of course he does, obviously.
So what kind of person is he?

127
00:07:53,320 --> 00:08:00,680
Well, I don't know the details either. He's just lived for business,
and I hear he has no wife or children.

128
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:06,340
Right, I heard that when he passes away, he'll donate
all his fortune to charitable institutions. Right?

129
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:12,680
How much is his fortune? I'd guess it's
not just one or two trillion yen, right?

130
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:17,620
When the amounts get that big,
you don't feel anything anymore.

131
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:21,760
Ten or twenty thousand yen is what
really gets your heart racing, right?

132
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:29,400
Listen, Ryo, make absolutely sure you don't make any blunders.
He's already on his way up.

133
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:30,880
Nii.

134
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:42,660
Listen, don't you dare screw this up.

135
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:48,440
Hello. Grandpa, is your back better now?

136
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:54,180
Don't go casually calling him
"grandpa." Pardon my rudeness, sir.

137
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:57,880
We're about to start filming. Yes.

138
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:01,980
Do your job properly.

139
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:07,580
Right.

140
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:11,700
Don't yawn.

141
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:15,060
Now we're going live.

142
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:17,060
3

143
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:18,040
2

144
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:20,020
Hold still.

145
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:21,860
Don't scratch your head.

146
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:23,520
Pull yourself together, you idiot!

147
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:25,060
Ugh, you're so annoying.

148
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:26,600
Just leave me alone, will you?

149
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,860
You stubborn old goat.

150
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:30,820
What do you mean, "stubborn old man"?

151
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:33,540
I called you a stubborn
old man because you are one.

152
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:36,620
What did you say?
It's because you don't do your job properly.

153
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:39,640
But that's true,
you're always nagging, nag, nag, nag.

154
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:41,980
Being told that all the time,
I lose all motivation.

155
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:43,720
You're nagging like that all the time.

156
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:46,280
Alright, roll the camera and film those two.

157
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:46,760
Yes.

158
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:47,560
I'm not nagging.

159
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:50,180
You are, you stubborn old man.

160
00:09:50,180 --> 00:09:53,560
It's because you always
cause me so much worry.

161
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,740
That's the unnecessary part.

162
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:57,580
I'm a fully grown adult now, you know.

163
00:09:57,580 --> 00:10:01,720
What! You don't understand a parent's heart at all.
That's exactly what I mean!

164
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,920
Enough! Just leave me alone already!

165
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:07,980
So the Chief ended up appearing in it too?

166
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:11,620
No, the director really liked my acting,
you know.

167
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:13,900
They changed the content at the last minute.

168
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,403
If it's you and the Chief,

169
00:10:15,453 --> 00:10:18,480
it's just like your everyday exchanges at the police box,
isn't it.

170
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,580
Well, yeah.

171
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:23,560
Isn't it about time for the commercial?

172
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:24,280
Yeah.

173
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,900
This is it.

174
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,740
It's really well made.

175
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:32,100
Haha, he's parted his hair and everything.

176
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:32,980
Shut up.

177
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:35,140
The Chief's come on screen too.

178
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:38,100
You look pretty good on TV.

179
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:41,760
Wow, neither of them looks like
someone who'd bring bad luck.

180
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:43,760
Mm, well, yeah.

181
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:51,820
Are you alright?

182
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,240
You're not hurt, are you?

183
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,120
I'm fine.

184
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,680
It's a pretty good commercial, isn't it?

185
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:03,340
Really.

186
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:04,280
Police officer recruitment.

187
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:11,860
Me and the Chief as father and son?

188
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:13,960
I'm not joking.

189
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:17,400
Who'd ever want to be the
father of an idiot like this?

190
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:19,920
I'm not joking either, you know.

191
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:23,260
But how did it end up like this, I wonder?

192
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:24,920
How would I know that?

193
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:27,340
Anyway, it's you, you see...

194
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:29,160
No, it's the Chief, you see...

195
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:32,460
If nothing happens like this,
it'd be fine...

196
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:36,280
I've got a bad feeling about this.

197
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,400
Eeeeh!

198
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:51,680
Are you telling me to become a real
father and son with Ryotsu like this?

199
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,620
Absolutely not!

200
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,740
The father of a man like this?

201
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:57,060
Look at this.

202
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:03,240
We've gone too far to back out now.

203
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,060
But, well...

204
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:11,120
No, I'm not saying you have
to stay father and son forever.

205
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:13,640
Just until the fuss dies down.

206
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:16,600
It's just a lie, Ohara.

207
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:19,400
But telling a lie...

208
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:23,780
If this gets out,
the police's credibility will plummet.

209
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:26,920
And then, you'll be held responsible!

210
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:30,660
Understood, Ohara?

211
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:31,680
Yes.

212
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:33,940
Ryotsu, you understand too, right?

213
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:40,340
And there's one more troublesome matter.

214
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:43,360
One more, you say?

215
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:48,220
The wealthy man wants to
invite you two to his home.

216
00:12:48,220 --> 00:12:50,200
You two, as father and son.

217
00:13:01,420 --> 00:13:02,620
Listen, Ryotsu.

218
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,820
Once you walk through these gates,

219
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,600
you and I are father and son.

220
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:09,300
We're not Chief and Ryotsu anymore, got it?

221
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,520
I know, I know.

222
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:12,840
Daddy.

223
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:15,260
Kankichi.

224
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:18,540
It's like I'm having a bad dream.

225
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:21,560
Honestly, this rich man...

226
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:25,100
The moment I laid eyes on you two,
I was certain of it.

227
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:27,800
This is truly a father and son.

228
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:32,000
There's a bond between parent and child that can't be hidden,
no matter how hard you try.

229
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,960
Y-yes, thank you.

230
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:37,820
Well, don't be so stiff.
Please, make yourselves at home.

231
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:42,600
Well, I've devoted myself single-mindedly to work all my life,
never touching play or gambling,

232
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:45,380
considering them unthinkable.
I've lived 80 years that way.

233
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:48,280
Lately, I've had moments
when I suddenly feel lonely.

234
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:52,380
With people like you two,
a father and son of Japan,

235
00:13:52,380 --> 00:13:55,740
I've always wanted to sit down and have a good,
long talk.

236
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:56,184
Now, then,

237
00:13:56,234 --> 00:13:59,860
please, both of you,
think of this as your own home and relax.

238
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:01,060
Y-yeah.

239
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:05,400
Easier said than done. We're just so tense.

240
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:14,500
H-hey, Ryotsu!
What an embarrassing thing to do!

241
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:16,440
B-but, Chief!

242
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,640
Ryotsu... Chief?

243
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:21,260
No, Ryo, Ryo

244
00:14:21,310 --> 00:14:23,700
You're supposed to use both hands,
aren't you?

245
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:25,800
Y-yes, right.

246
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:26,840
Hmm

247
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:30,820
Don't do embarrassing things, Kan, Kankichi.

248
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:33,330
B-but, pa-pa-pa-pa, th-

249
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:35,660
This teacup is 200,000 yen...
the price tag says so.

250
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,820
W-what?!

251
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:41,460
What?

252
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:43,740
Everything has a price tag stuck on it.

253
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:45,840
Even on the tropical fish.

254
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,552
Hahaha,

255
00:14:47,602 --> 00:14:52,480
so you can always tell what things are worth,
we've put list prices on them.

256
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:54,840
Is this one priced at this too?

257
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:58,080
Of course, everything is an honest price.

258
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,140
Haa...

259
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,002
He's lived for nothing but business,

260
00:15:02,052 --> 00:15:04,580
and apparently he has no wife or children.

261
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:09,080
I heard that when he dies, he'll donate
all his assets to a care facility.

262
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,210
No children,

263
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,660
and more money than he could ever spend.

264
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:20,000
If I play my cards right,
I might get some of that money...

265
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:25,920
Idiot! What if a 250,000 yen one breaks?

266
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,720
It's 200,000 yen, you know.

267
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:30,980
Hurry up and wipe it!
This carpet is 10 million yen!

268
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:37,060
Truly, one can only imagine the hardship your father
went through raising Kankichi-kun to be who he is today.

269
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:44,520
Well, yes, this idiot son of mine
has given me nothing but trouble.

270
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:49,320
You can say that,
but you can't hide how close you two are.

271
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,500
I heard you two went to the
Edogawa area together the other day.

272
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,340
Edogawa? Well, no...

273
00:15:56,160 --> 00:16:01,320
You know, the other day, during the Shimete-haihan investigation,
you two went to Edogawa together.

274
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:05,060
Now that you mention it, we did.

275
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:11,820
You went to Edogawa again during work to bet on the boats,
didn't you?

276
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:16,540
Uh-oh, if that gambling-hating old
man finds out about the boat racing...

277
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,440
What was he like when he was little?

278
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,820
Well, what kind of child was Kankichi?

279
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:26,580
He was top of the class in his studies,
and always at the head of the class.

280
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:28,262
I wish that were true, though.

281
00:16:28,312 --> 00:16:31,620
Even back in elementary school, at sports day,
it was always a contest over who'd come in first.

282
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:37,480
There was a mosquito.

283
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,100
A mosquito?

284
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,380
No, it was a fly.

285
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:46,160
A fly? Flies come from... flies.

286
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:49,680
There was a fly, Papa.

287
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,840
W-a bee oh.

288
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:55,060
It'd be terrible if Papa got stung.

289
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:58,280
What a kind thing to say.

290
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:00,420
Of course, Papa.

291
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,940
Thank you, Kankichi.

292
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:04,500
Yeah, this is great after all.

293
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:09,320
Kankichi, Kankichi.

294
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,800
What a beautiful sight.

295
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:17,280
The image of a Japanese father and son,
right here.

296
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:19,360
I'm deeply moved, I am.

297
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:22,420
Let's take a bath together.

298
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:26,860
A bath, is it?

299
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:28,860
Why a bath?

300
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:31,220
Scrubbing each other's backs.

301
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:33,820
The bath is the very origin of
the bond between father and son.

302
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:36,580
Like this, naked and bare,

303
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:38,360
as we were born,

304
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:41,280
hiding nothing as we talk
with our sons and grandsons.

305
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:43,760
This was my ideal.

306
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:46,960
Pa-pa-pa-pa

307
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,540
I'll wash your back for you.

308
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:54,160
Then I'll wash Mr. Kanemochida's back.

309
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:55,760
I see.

310
00:17:58,220 --> 00:18:00,220
Dad's back is so broad.

311
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:03,420
Don't say such creepy things.

312
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:06,840
Because Dad is a man with
a heart as broad as his back.

313
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:09,140
You don't sweat the small stuff, do you?

314
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:11,700
I see.

315
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:15,420
So you want Ryotsu to forget that he went to the boat races,
is that it?

316
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:16,740
That won't do.

317
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:18,560
Hey, Mr. Kanemochida...

318
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:25,780
Scolding them when they do wrong is only natural for a parent, isn't it?
Of course it is.

319
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:30,080
Like, say, during work hours, you know.

320
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:34,820
Hey, harder.

321
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:37,300
Okay, Dad.

322
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,940
Let me take over, Kankichi.

323
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:50,720
Noooo!

324
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,480
You always liked hot baths, didn't you?

325
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:11,380
If you don't get in up to your shoulders,
you'll catch a cold.

326
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:23,820
Papa, let's take a bath together too!

327
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,020
Whaaaaat?

328
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:33,740
They really get along well.

329
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,200
Ugh, how sweet.

330
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:43,200
Now then, a drink after the bath!

331
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,820
Don't hold back, go right ahead.

332
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:46,460
Sake

333
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:47,500
No, this won't do.

334
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:49,140
If Ryotsu gets some sake in him...

335
00:19:49,140 --> 00:20:05,180


336
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:06,800
I often think, you know,

337
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:10,700
how wonderful it would be to have
sons and grandsons like you two.

338
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:14,120
Honesty is the best policy.

339
00:20:14,580 --> 00:20:17,820
That's been my motto for eighty years.

340
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:22,100
But the people who lie the most are
the ones who claim to be the most honest.

341
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:26,720
Honesty is the best policy

342
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:30,460
That's a phrase this guy
has never been familiar with.

343
00:20:32,140 --> 00:20:34,860
But what about me

344
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,740
A lie is fine, Ohara.

345
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:41,340
If this gets out,
the police's credibility will plummet.

346
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:44,560
If that happens, Gay,
it'll be a question of responsibility!

347
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:49,740
Actually, Mr. Kanemochida,

348
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:50,060
right?

349
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:53,460
No, speaking of fathers, at our police box

350
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:56,560
there's a boss named Ohara.

351
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:58,880
This boss is an incredible nag.

352
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:04,100
He yells
"You idiot!" over and over, like that's the only word he knows.

353
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:09,320
Calling an idiot an idiot,
though, anyone can do that.

354
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:13,620
Right? You'd think so too.
Gramps, you really get it.

355
00:21:13,620 --> 00:21:15,740
Hey, Ryo! Kankichi!

356
00:21:15,740 --> 00:21:18,020
Dad, be quiet! Dad!

357
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:23,960
But you know, I don't say it out loud,
but I'm grateful to that man.

358
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,900
There's love in his idiocy.

359
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:30,180
Like a father's manuscript.

360
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:37,820
Honestly,
I'm not a very excellent police officer.

361
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:39,420
I have plenty of reprimand reports too.

362
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:42,100
I even play pachinko and
go to the races on duty.

363
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:46,120
But every time he calls me an idiot,

364
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:48,780
I think of Papa, right here.

365
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:51,800
Look, Papa always says it, doesn't he?

366
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:53,820
Even when pounding rice cakes,
don't tell lies.

367
00:21:53,820 --> 00:21:55,780
Honesty over fasting.

368
00:21:55,780 --> 00:21:58,940
So I hide nothing from him,

369
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:00,500
and I blurt it all out.

370
00:22:01,260 --> 00:22:02,020
Impressive.

371
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,960
What an honest young man he is!

372
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:05,780
Father.

373
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:07,020
Kankichi-kun,

374
00:22:07,020 --> 00:22:10,240
could we not have
Kankichi-kun as an adopted son?

375
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:12,180
A-adopted son?!

376
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:14,000
I'm afraid I must decline.

377
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:17,900
I have the responsibility of
looking after this Papa of mine.

378
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,400
I like him even more now.

379
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:21,680
Please, please, I'd be delighted.

380
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:24,620
We did it! Operation a complete success!

381
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:29,280
Please raise your head, Mr. Kanemochida.

382
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:32,860
It is I who should be bowing my head.

383
00:22:34,540 --> 00:22:36,480
I am truly sorry.

384
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:39,960
I have done something
against the way of man.

385
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:45,640
It was all a lie.

386
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:46,940
Bejō!

387
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:48,480
No, Papa.

388
00:22:49,140 --> 00:22:50,680
That's enough, Ryotsu.

389
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:55,080
This man and I are not
father and son at all.

390
00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:56,500
We're complete strangers.

391
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,100
How could you say that, Papa!

392
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:02,220
I'm the boss this man
has been talking about.

393
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:06,660
For the sake of the police's reputation, we've
been pretending to be father and son until now.

394
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:08,300
W-what, what, what?!

395
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:10,020
No, no, that's not true.

396
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:13,400
Papa has a habit of saying
senseless things when he gets going.

397
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:15,500
Look, we even look just alike, don't we?

398
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:17,720
Huh?

399
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:19,800
I've been a fool.

400
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:24,760
I've been jolted awake by this man, the one I usually shout
"idiot, idiot" at.

401
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:26,320
Papa, starry-eyed.

402
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:36,440
I sincerely apologize for all
the trouble we've caused you.

403
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:39,420
This man and I are complete strangers.

404
00:23:39,420 --> 00:23:40,860
I'm sorry.

405
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:42,060
Sorry.

406
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:43,840
I'm sorry.

407
00:23:43,840 --> 00:23:45,200
Sorry.

408
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:46,820
I'm sorry.

409
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,080
Sorry.

410
00:23:52,380 --> 00:23:57,820
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out,

411
00:23:59,100 --> 00:24:04,480
walking while looking back,
led by the hand by Gaaja.

412
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:11,040
That strange feeling I had back then,

413
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:16,900
so on the tiles of the arcade street,

414
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:22,680
I tried walking only on the black ones.

415
00:24:25,180 --> 00:24:30,920
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

416
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:34,940
Pompous-faced politicians,

417
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:38,280
and blue-eyeshadowed aunties too.

418
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:43,880
Try turning that corner over there,

419
00:24:44,820 --> 00:24:49,400
and you'll meet everyone, everyone!

420
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:57,020
Over there, Kame-ari! Surely Kame-ari!

421
00:24:58,320 --> 00:25:02,200
Everyone, come on over to our town!

422
00:25:04,500 --> 00:25:10,180
Over there, Kame-ari! Surely Kame-ari!

423
00:25:11,520 --> 00:25:15,400
Everyone, come on over to our town!

424
00:25:16,460 --> 00:25:16,960
Thank you.

425
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:24,840
They say I go around lecturing
the young folks in town.

426
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:27,220
Do I really look like such an old geezer?

427
00:25:27,220 --> 00:25:28,500
Do you think so?

428
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:33,080
Understood.
I'll prove my innocence, just you watch.

429
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:36,860
See you next time, okay?

430
00:25:45,940 --> 00:25:46,420
Thank you.

